														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1733451">
									

<p>I see two major differences between this and 1733.</p>
<p>One, there's an implication that they might actually be influencing something outside the videotape. I'd kind of like this to be more clear - are they really murdering people? Or is it all just images? &quot;The Foundation doesn't know&quot; is a valid answer, but if that's the case, it seems like it should be more explicit.</p>
<p>Two, 1733 is involuntary and wants it to stop; these are voluntary and want it to continue. I think that's kind of an interesting take on the idea, although I'm not sure if it's enough of a twist to justify a separate article.</p>
<p>There is of course a natural question: if both exist in the same universe, are they manifestations of the same underlying anomaly? Obviously, this should not actually be answered in the text.</p>

							</div>

								
					
